# The Escalation Cost - repository ignore rules
#
# The project-local data store lives OUTSIDE this repo, git-ignored by location:
#   C:\Users\jaek9\Documents\LaggingTruth\The-Escalation-Cost
# Raw data is never committed. The repo data layer (data/SOURCES.md, data/pull.py)
# is documentation-only. analysis/outputs/*.json ARE committed (do not ignore them).

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Raw data formats (never committed; live in the project-local store)
*.csv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.parquet
data/raw/

# Rendered manuscript - a DERIVED artifact, regenerated by analysis/render_paper.py
# from the manuscript + claims.lock and never committed. Ignored by name rather
# than merely left untracked, because on a sibling paper three stale rendered
# files were swept into a commit by `git add -A` rename-detection and caught only
# in staging review before the tag.
paper/*.rendered.md

# Suite/validation byproducts. These are written by the experiment scripts' own
# --suite (mechanism-validation) modes, NOT by a real run: no ledger row reads
# them, and they regenerate on demand from the committed suite code. The suite's
# evidence is that committed code plus its ALL-PASS output recorded on the phase
# task. Named exceptions to the "analysis/outputs/*.json ARE committed" rule
# above, which governs EXPERIMENT RESULTS.
analysis/outputs/*_suite_check.json
analysis/outputs/*_suite_smoke.json

# Local scratch
scratch/
tmp/
review_package_the_escalation_cost.zip

# Phase 5a review-package build products (assembled on demand by
# verification/build_review_package.py - never committed)
review_package/
the-escalation-cost_review_package.zip
